Engrave the same piece as piece.mid into publisher-level piece.pdf via LilyPond. The written beat grid lives in compose_piece.py (phrases A, A2, B, CODA and LH_A, LH_B, LH_CODA) and is already dumped as piece.ly by engrave_piece.py (widget piano_score). That dump is one line of raw skips, a dynamics voice, and pedal marks — not a publisher engraving. Rewrite the LilyPond source as a readable grand-staff piano score of those written pitches and rhythms (key of A-flat major, 4/4, melody over accompaniment, title Nocturne), compile it with LilyPond to piece.pdf, and leave the probe piece_pdf_built able to read true: non-empty PDF of at least one page from that .ly, note sequence matching the written piece (not the performance leans in piece.mid). Do not OCR the page. A missing PDF, a failed compile, or a score of a different piece reads false. Need:3 — a pianist reading the score would play it as written and find nothing to correct. Non-goals: no quotation; no notes or write-up files; do not optically recognize the PDF.
