Measure the written piece in compose_piece.py and the performance in piece.mid: duration in seconds via the tempo map, whether it is melody over a bass-plus-pattern accompaniment, how many distinct phrases, whether the melody quotes a known romantic theme, velocity standard deviation, tempo-event count, CC64 transition count, and the fraction of onsets more than 20 ms off a 16th grid. Sources are compose_piece.py and piece.mid only.
performance piece written melody note romantic single accompaniment alone beat between block
piece mid lasts between 60 and 180 seconds of performed time  the span of a short romantic character piece 
the written piece is melody over accompaniment  one upper line against a left hand pattern  not a single voice and not block chords alone 
the written piece is a closed form of several phrases  not one unvaried loop 
the written melody is original  it is not a known romantic theme 
the performance s note velocities vary the way a player s touch does  not a single sequencer value 
the performance has a tempo map  not one tempo for the whole file 
