Compose an original short piano piece and save it as piece.mid only (no notes, plan, or write-up). One major key. Right hand: a monophonic line you could hum (at least eight notes, mostly steps and small skips), in at least two phrases separated by a rest of at least one beat, ending on the tonic on a downbeat with the bass on that same tonic. Left hand: a broken-chord figure that keeps moving under the tune — one note at a time, each bar spelling a triad or seventh, the same rhythm repeating, no gap longer than a beat while the melody is present. The tune louder than the left hand, and each phrase arched in velocity (the loudest note neither first nor last, phrases of at least four notes). Piano only, GM program 0, no drums or other programs. No quotation of an existing piece; every pitch and rhythm is chosen, not generated at random. Put the melody and the left hand on separable channels so a probe can tell them apart. While writing, measure the unknowns on piece.mid.
