Write piece.mid: a short original four-voice chorale for piano in a minor key. Four voices throughout, two to a hand (soprano and alto right, tenor and bass left), ending on a proper cadence (V or V7 to i) with all four voices on the final chord. Voice leading a teacher would pass: no parallel perfect fifths or octaves, common tones kept in the same voice and octave, no voice crossing. The soprano carries the melody (moves more than the inner voices, stays on top). Sustain pedal (CC64) resets at each chord change and is not held across a harmony change. Piano only: program 0, no percussion, no other programs. Every pitch and rhythm is a composed decision — no random note generation, no quotation of an existing piece. The piece is the only deliverable: do not write notes, plans, or write-ups. While the file is in hand, probe it for voice_count, two_per_hand, minor_key, proper_ending, parallel_perfect_count, common_tone_kept, no_voice_crossing, top_voice_carries, pedal_follows_harmony, piano_only, and piece_mid_exists.
