Write piece.mid, an original short piano nocturne, and measure it. Wide rolling left hand: bass on the low onset of each bar, chord tones above it, span wide, compound time (6/8, 9/8, or 12/8) with a non-overlapping eighth-note roll. Right hand a singing line above the left, with a couple of ornamental stepwise runs. Accompaniment stays under the melody in register and velocity; sustain pedal resets when the left-hand harmony changes. Piano only, program 0, no percussion or other programs. Melodies are your own, not a quotation; every pitch and rhythm is chosen, not random. Do not write notes, plans, or write-up files.
