Write piece.mid: nine bars, one chord per bar, block chords in both hands on I vi IV V, twice, then I, in one stated major key. Piano only (program 0, no percussion). Pedal each chord down with the attack and lift cleanly before the next change, never smeared across a harmony. Shape a crescendo through bars 1-4 (each bar at least 6 velocity louder than the last) and a diminuendo through bars 5-8 (each at least 6 softer), with bar 9 the softest of all and at least 20% longer than the steady tempo of bars 1-8 (those eight within 2% of each other). Original voicing only — no quotation. No notes, plan, or write-up files. Measure every unknown above from piece.mid while you build it.
