Compose piece.mid (piano only, GM program 0, no other programs or percussion): a short piece whose every pitch and rhythm is chosen, not random and not a quotation. One story — a feeling stated at the start (an opening pitch-interval statement), something that unsettles it in the middle (bass leaves the opening home), and a resolution that comes late rather than early (opening shape and home bass return in the latter part and the last bass is home). One high point, not four: a single intensity peak with everything else subordinate, and a stillness (a span at most a quarter of peak intensity) wholly before that peak or wholly after it. Read the arc off the file with one instrument: per-beat intensity (velocity times sounding duration) showing where it rises, where it empties, and where it peaks, and run that same peak rule on a flat control and a four-equal-peaks control so the counts separate. No notes, plan, or write-up files.
intensity global length peak first sounding piece pitch span bass beats class
