Write and play piece.mid: an original homorhythmic chord sequence for piano (program 0 only), four notes to a chord and two to a hand, so the top voice is a melody of the worker's own. Voice every chord so the top note is the highest and strictly louder than the other three, with the left hand strictly below the right. Join the melody as one line (each top note meets or overlaps the next). Place the chords beneath it — the three lower notes of a chord are not struck at one velocity. Change the sustain pedal with every harmony: down with the chord, clean off before the next, never across a change. No quotation, no random pitches, and no notes or write-up files.
chord melody note notes chords above across next other velocity beneath between
