Write piece.mid: a short chord progression (four to sixteen harmonies, each a chord) played piano-only so it sounds like hands and feet, not a sequencer. Pedal holds through each harmony and clears at every change, never smeared across one. Loudness grows and then recedes; the closing harmony is strictly the softest and the slowest. Read those facts off piece.mid — pedal against the harmony boundaries, and per-harmony velocity and span — so a file pedalled through the changes or played at one level would fail. Melodies are your own, not a quotation; every pitch and rhythm is a decision; no notes or write-up files.
harmony file down pedal strictly cc64 chord close earlier falls false last
piece mid exists in the project root and parses as a standard midi file containing note events 
the file is piano only  program 0 on the sounding channel  no other programs  percussion channel unused 
the piece is a short chord progression  between four and sixteen successive harmonies  each a chord of three or more distinct pitch classes sounding together  not a single line and not one chord for the whole file 
the sound is held through each harmony  sustain pedal  cc64  is down while that harmony s notes sound 
the pedal is cleared at every harmony change and never smeared across one  cc64 goes up before the next harmony attacks  and is not still down from the previous harmony into the next 
loudness grows and recedes the way a phrase breathes  some harmony after the first is strictly louder than the opening  and a later harmony falls strictly below that peak  so the shape is neither flat  nor only rising  nor only falling 
Write an original singing phrase to project-root piece.mid and play it with rubato a probe can read back. Piano only: program 0, one instrument, no percussion channel, no other programs. The melody is the worker's own — no quotation, and no random pitch or rhythm. One monophonic upper line of at least eight notes, mostly steps and small leaps, over a simple accompaniment that stays strictly below it in pitch whenever they sound together and quieter than it on average. Shape the line by touch: the melody note at the highest pitch is the fullest, at least 8 MIDI velocity units above the mean of the other melody notes. Bend time in the file itself (tempo map or realized beat spans, not a note beside the file): the bar holding that melodic peak is stretched to at least 1.2 times the median beat of the other bars, the last bar slows by that same margin and is not the peak bar, and every remaining beat stays within 8 percent of that body median. At least four bars, with at least four body beats. The piece is the only file to add.
bars body mean note beat median performed duration last least melody peak
