Read piece.mid as it stands — do not rewrite it. Against the four phrases (peaks at bars 2, 8, 11, 13) and the fifteen harmonies already known, measure: how many phrases stretch at their own peak, how many slow into their last bar, the smallest peak-velocity margin inside a phrase, whether phrase-peak velocities are one monotonic ramp, the fraction of harmony changes where the pedal clears, and the fraction of harmonies the pedal holds. Also record the upper-voice pitch sequence and the harmony bass-pitch-class sequence as the identity a later performance must keep. Use the piano-line and pedal/loudness instruments already in the library; a reading must be false on a strict-time, flat-velocity, or pedal-through-changes file.
